        },
        {
          "category": "shortcut_resistance",
          "evidence": "All288 newly committed branch choices are true, all456 new child entries pass initiation and all504 child returns pass success. Failures are confined to root I/S; selected suspended guards can be currently false, which is a different real resumption mechanism.",
          "fix": "Add matched executed else choices, nonroot entry/exit failures and terminal checkpoints to a separate prospective batch; handmade test coverage is not corpus coverage.",
          "issue_id": "true_branch_child_success_only",
          "nonblocking_reason": "The nine public pilot contexts require root guard contrasts and retained-selection behavior, both actually witnessed. Broader child-failure/else coverage is explicitly unestablished.",
          "severity": "moderate"
        },
        {
          "category": "shortcut_resistance",
          "evidence": "120/216 completed and24 each paused/initiation_failed/success_failed/invalid. Fitted status majority/mode/history cues reach55.56%, and budget or mode/history/budget reaches66.67%; only75 full outputs occur among108 semantic tasks. These are corpus diagnostics, not learner results.",
          "fix": "Use full typed target evaluation, report conditional tables and redundancy, and cross outcome statuses with varied valid modes/budgets/history lengths prospectively.",
          "issue_id": "status_and_output_redundancy",
          "nonblocking_reason": "A status heuristic does not reproduce the full events, bindings, checkpoint and next-event object for complex rows. Public design already scopes this finite controlled pilot rather than a shortcut-free benchmark.",
          "severity": "moderate"
        },
        {
          "category": "generalization_value",
          "evidence": "Four exposed-dev families (indices18,19,28,29) share primitive motifs and the same interruption core with eight train families. The legacy24 views collapse to8 graph signatures, while twelve new families are distinct in all three own normalizations with zero legacy collisions. This is structural separation, not empirical transfer or independent-model evidence.",
          "fix": "Preserve family-level splits and public exposure labels; later preregister a held-out composition/state/cut study. Do not infer model improvement from these data.",
          "issue_id": "exposed_dev_and_finite_programs",
          "nonblocking_reason": "All descendants of each family remain in one split and actual graph novelty is truthful at the published normalization. The narrow interpreter-training use remains supported.",
          "severity": "moderate"
        }
      ],
